  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-paper-design",
      "text": "Paper Design MCP bridge as a [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) bundle.\n\nConnects to the **Paper Desktop** MCP server (`http://127.0.0.1:29979/mcp`), registers every Paper tool as a native `paper_*` tool with image screenshot support, injects Cursor-parity design guidance, registers the Paper skills, and exposes reconnect + OAuth auth commands."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it provides",
      "text": "- **`paper_*` tools** — every tool advertised by Paper Desktop MCP (`get_basic_info`, `get_screenshot`, `write_html`, `update_styles`, …), registered natively on `ctx.tools`. Raw MCP `inputSchema`s are normalized to the enforced DSH JSON-Schema subset (`$schema`/`format`/`pattern`/`propertyNames`/`min*`/`max*` stripped, `anyOf`→`oneOf`).\n- **Image screenshot forwarding** — `get_screenshot` image blocks are decoded and durably committed through `ctx.attachments` (`saveImage`), then emitted as attachment-backed image blocks (and deferred as plugin-sourced context for nested `run_code` dispatches), so screenshots reach image-capable models.\n- **Cursor-parity guidance** — standing rules injected as a system-prompt section (order 150), plus the full `paper-mcp-instructions` guide injected for the first 2 agent turns after connect/reconnect. `paper_get_guide` also caches the guide body.\n- **Skills** — `code-to-design`, `design-to-code` (Cursor Paper plugin bodies verbatim), and `paper-design` (progressive-disclosure tool reference index).\n- **`/paper-reconnect`** — re-initializes the MCP session, **(re)registers the `paper_*` tools**, clears the guide cache, and resets the early-turn gui"
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- **Paper Desktop** running with a file open (the MCP server lives inside the desktop app). It does not have to be running when DSH boots — the bridge picks it up when it appears.\n- **DSH** `0.2.0-rc.2` or `0.1.0-rc.5`+ — the plugin declares matching `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` peer ranges, and DSH refuses to load it on a runtime outside them.\n- A DeepSeek Harness profile that bundles `@deepseek-ai/dsh-base` (or the services it mounts): `tools`, `systemPrompt`, `attachments` (for images), `skills`, `commands`, `llm`.\n- An image-capable model route for screenshot support (text tools work on any route)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Add this package to the profile and its `bundles` list, e.g. in `~/.dsh/profiles/<name>/package.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@try-works/dsh-paper-design\": \"^0.1.6\"\n  },\n\nThen `pnpm install` in the profile and restart the running DSH process. The bridge ships its `src/*.ts` sources directly (DSH loads them through `tsx`), mirroring `dsh-recursive-mode`.\n\n> Restart is required for host/bundle changes: the web client-plugin HMR only rebuilds the web shell, not host plugins."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "- Ask the agent to read or design in Paper; it will use `paper_get_basic_info`, `paper_open_file`, `paper_get_screenshot`, and the rest.\n- `/paper-reconnect` republishes the tools and re-syncs after restarting Paper Desktop. You normally do not need it: the tools appear on their own when Paper starts.\n- `/paper-auth-status` / `/paper-auth-login` / `/paper-auth-logout` manage OAuth auth when a server requires it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm install\npnpm run build                        # type-check (tsc -p tsconfig.build.json)\npnpm run verify                       # live MCP bridge verification (needs Paper Desktop)\npnpm run verify:bridge                # in-process plugin boot + live paper_get_basic_info"
    },
    {
      "section": "Layout",
      "text": "- `src/index.ts` — bundle entry: register prompt/skills/commands, then connect, normalize, and (re)register tools with late-start retry.\n- `src/mcp-client.ts` — minimal Streamable HTTP MCP client (initialize/tools-list/tools-call, session tracking, SSE parsing, one-shot re-init, bearer-token + challenge hooks).\n- `src/auth.ts` — discovery-driven MCP OAuth 2.1 client (RFC 8414/OIDC discovery, DCR, PKCE, loopback redirect, token exchange/refresh, persisted store, challenge handling).\n- `src/schema.ts` — raw Paper JSON Schema → enforced DSH subset normalizer.\n- `src/guide.ts` — standing rules + early-turn guide markers and builder.\n- `src/skills.ts` — runtime skill registrations.\n- `skills/*/SKILL.md` — on-disk skill bodies (parity artifacts).\n- `cordis.patch.yml` — loader patch inserting the bridge into a `cordis:group` realm."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
